  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 91036662a85844eb162bdfbe2ea8ce9c, type: 3}
  m_Name: TurkishRules
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  displayName: Turkish
  description: Dama - pieces move in straight lines on every square, flying kings, mandatory capture, no immediate 180-degree reversal mid-chain.
  longDescription: "<b><color=#D4AF37>Goal:</color></b>\nCapture all of your opponent's pieces, or leave them with no legal move to make.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Board:</color></b>\nPlayed on an 8x8 board, but every square is used - not just the dark ones. Each player starts with 16 pieces filling the 2nd and 3rd rows on their side, leaving the very back row empty. White always moves first.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Movement:</color></b>\nPieces move orthogonally only - no diagonals. Men move one square forward, left, or right, but capture in all four directions, including backward. The Dama (king) slides any distance in a straight line and can fly across empty squares to capture from range.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Capturing:</color></b>\nCapturing is mandatory, and if more than one path is available, you must play the one that captures the most pieces. Captured pieces are removed immediately, which can open up new paths mid-turn. Within one turn, you also can't reverse straight back through the square you just left.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Kings:</color></b>\nA piece only crowns if it finishes its turn on the back row - a man with a further legal capture keeps playing as a man rather than promoting mid-chain.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Win:</color></b>\nCapture every enemy piece, leave your opponent with no legal move, or win instantly by reducing them to one regular piece while you still have at least one Dama.\n\n<b><color=#D4AF37>Draw:</color></b>\nEither player may offer a draw at any time; if accepted, the match ends level. The match is also drawn if the same position repeats three times, or the instant both sides are reduced to exactly one piece each - unless that one piece is a lone man against a Dama, which wins outright instead of drawing."
  rows: 8
  columns: 8
  pieceRowsPerSide: 2
  movementScheme: 1
  piecesOnAllSquares: 1
  leaveBackRowEmpty: 1
  flyingKings: 1
  menCaptureBackward: 1
  menCannotCaptureKings: 0
  mustCaptureMaximum: 1
  preferKingMover: 0
  preferKingCaptures: 0
  preferEarlierKingCapture: 0
  midChainPromotionRule: 0
  deferCaptureRemoval: 0
  forbidImmediateReversal: 1
  noProgressMoveLimit: 0
  singleManLosesToKing: 1
  firstMoveColor: 1
  threefoldRepetitionEnabled: 1
  threeVsOneKingDrawLimit: 0
  twoVsOneKingDrawLimit: 0
  oneVsOneIsDraw: 1
